# Client Component Patterns

All client components (marked with `'use client';`) should follow these patterns:

## List Components
Example: [app/(authenticated)/claimed/gift-list.tsx](mdc:app/(authenticated)/claimed/gift-list.tsx)

1. Use `useOptimistic` for state management https://react.dev/reference/react/useOptimistic
2. Use `startTransition` for UI updates https://react.dev/reference/react/startTransition
3. Handle actions with direct function call if possible, use validated forms https://react.dev/reference/react/useActionState
4. Provide proper error handling and reversion to initial state 
5. Use consistent UI patterns from shadcn/ui

## Form Handling
Don't use `useFormStatus` directly. Instead:

1. Create dedicated button/form components with their own hooks
2. Or use optimistic UI patterns with `useOptimistic` and `startTransition`

## Data Fetching
Data should be fetched in server components when possible, then passed to client components as props.

## Naming Conventions
- `handle*` - Client-side action handlers (e.g., `handleUnclaim`)
- `*List` - Components that display lists (e.g., `GiftList`)
- Use PascalCase for component names
- Use camelCase for variables and functions

# UI Patterns

## Link Patterns

For list items with multiple links:

1. Make entire cells clickable for better UX
2. Use `stopPropagation()` for nested links
3. Add hover effects for visual feedback

Example from [app/(authenticated)/gifts/gift-list.tsx](mdc:app/(authenticated)/gifts/gift-list.tsx):

```jsx
<Link href={`/gifts/${gift.id}`} className="space-y-1 hover:opacity-80">
  <div className="font-medium">{gift.name}</div>
  {/* Gift details */}
  
  {gift.url && (
    <a
      href={gift.url}
      onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}
      className="text-blue-500 hover:underline"
    >
      View Product
    </a>
  )}
</Link>
```

## List Components

When displaying lists of items:
1. Use consistent grid layouts with responsive variants
2. Show/hide columns based on viewport size
3. Include proper loading states with skeletons
